+# Solution
+
+`evaluate` uses memoized depth-first evaluation: each cell is computed on demand, so forward references and transitive dependency chains work regardless of dictionary order. A set of cells currently being evaluated detects both direct and indirect dependency cycles and raises `CycleError`.
+
+Formulas are handled by a small recursive-descent parser implementing the specified precedence and left associativity. It supports numbers, cell references, parentheses, insignificant whitespace, and recursive unary minus. All values are converted to `float`, while arithmetic uses Python's normal behavior, including `ZeroDivisionError` for division by zero.
